&lt;p&gt;OLLAMA DOWNLOAD PAGE&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Step Two - Downloading the Model&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;After downloading Ollama we need to access the program via our &lt;strong&gt;command line or terminal&lt;/strong&gt; (depending on the OS you’re using) I know this might sound confusing but I promise it sounds more complicated than it is. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;When you open your terminal type in “ollama” and press enter. You should see a list of commands signifying that you’ve done it correctly. While there are numerous ways to download it using that terminal here are two ways that may be a little bit easier for you!&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Through The Terminal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The three commands you need are:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="highlight js-code-highlight"&gt;
&lt;pre class="highlight jsx"&gt;&lt;code&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ollama&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;run&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ollama&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;list&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span class="nx"&gt;ollama&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;rm&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="p"&gt;[&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nx"&gt;model&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="nx"&gt;name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="p"&gt;]&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;

&lt;/div&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Before opening your terminal you want to figure out which model you want to use. Models can be found here, which is coincidentally the second way to download the models I mentioned. Providing you with a more detailed breakdown of the models and alternative ways to download said models.  &lt;/p&gt;


