&lt;p&gt;After running the “ollama run [model name]” command with the name of the model you want to download it will be available to be used via the same command after a few minutes depending on the size. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Feiub1ik13rjjti9ilchg.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Feiub1ik13rjjti9ilchg.png" alt=" " width="799" height="425"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;MICROSOFT POWERSHELL&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The other two commands, “ollama list” and “ollama rm [model name]” (with “rm” meaning remove), allow you to view all downloaded models and delete them as needed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;That’s all! You now have a local version of AI on your computer, though there’s a number of cool ways to expand upon this and turn your computer into an AI powered beast.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;


What is Open Source, Nous Research and XFRA, and Why It All Matters
&lt;/h2&gt;




&lt;p&gt;You’ve made it this far and you know how to utilize AI instead of using it so, what’s next? For the next three sections including the closing remarks I am going to teach you about open source projects showcasing some of the industry changing technology being built by independent developers and companies around the world, the effects of AI and what’s being done in the industry, and finally why learning more about AI in the first place is absolutely paramount to your future.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


What is Open Source?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open Source refers to software whose original source code is made publicly available for anyone to view, modify/enhance, and distribute. Furthermore, under the Open Source Initiative (OSI) there are more clearly defined criteria such as:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Free Redistribution:&lt;/strong&gt; Anyone can give away or sell the software without paying royalties or fees to the original creators.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Accessible Source Code:&lt;/strong&gt; The program must include the source code (the human-readable instructions written by programmers) or make it easily downloadable for free.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Allowed Modifications:&lt;/strong&gt; Anyone can modify the code to fix bugs, add new features, or adapt it for personal or commercial use. These modified versions are called "forks."&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;No Discrimination:&lt;/strong&gt; The software cannot restrict who uses it or what field of endeavor it is used in (e.g., it cannot ban commercial use or restrict use to certain industries).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;For years open source software has allowed individual contributors to create large scale projects that have shaped technology and the world as we know it today. These include Linux, one of the biggest OSs of all time as well as the backbone of modern technology, Chromium (the open source foundation behind Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, and Brave), and even AI companies such as Nous Research (more on them later). &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Open source technology is more than just a cool way to start a company, but a stand for transparency in the technology shaping our future and a supportive front for rapid innovation beyond a select few companies that control access. When the technology that shapes our societies and policies is kept secret and knowledge is limited to those who can afford it, it creates a dangerous precedent. So, what is being done out there to combat the consolidation of knowledge in the AI space?&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


Nous Research
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nous Research&lt;/strong&gt; is an applied AI research organization and a prominent leader in the open-source AI movement. Unlike traditional AI labs that keep their findings and models locked behind proprietary walls, Nous Research operates on a philosophy of radical transparency, public collaboration, and decentralization. WIth their core areas of focus being:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;State of the Art Open Models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Decentralized AI Training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Censorship Resistance &amp;amp; Open Access&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Not only do they pay researchers to publish findings vs other companies who do the opposite with a history of being open when it comes to information, this is a company I’ve been keeping an eye on when it comes to AI not just AI that works well but takes into consideration the policies and effects AI has on the broader community. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nous Research has also developed an interesting technology coined, “The Psyche Network”. An open, decentralized architecture designed to democratize AI development. Psyche connects underutilized or idle hardware from independent contributors worldwide to collectively train massive models. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Combining DisTrO (Distributed Training Over the Internet) and the Solana Blockchain the Psyche Network allows Nous Research to train their models over the internet via individual systems instead of data centers. Challenging the standard of AI development, while data centers are still the go to method this is a worthy avenue to research and develop due to the rising negative effects that data centers have in our communities. In addition to that the Solana Blockchain ensures that the training stays censorship free and prohibits one single entity from claiming ownership/control. Pioneering the ethical alternative to standard AI practices.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;


XFRA by SPAN
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fn6zfy9k9b45fdjnz6i37.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fn6zfy9k9b45fdjnz6i37.png" alt=" " width="800" height="404"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SPAN, XFRA INSTALLATION&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SPAN&lt;/strong&gt; is a startup out of California who is working on another alternative to training models and providing the compute needed for the rising AI demand. For generations AI compute is projected to outpace electrical generation creating a dangerous outlook for the future. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqsnkz832xhfd0qwwfi70.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fqsnkz832xhfd0qwwfi70.png" alt=" " width="800" height="729"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;GENERATION SUPPLY VS DEMAND CHART&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, what is SPAN betting on? XFRA. XFRA is a distributed compute cloud built from&lt;br&gt;
a fleet of XFRA Nodes deployed in homes and small businesses. Utilizing the excess energy that households are discarding to provide the energy that is needed to keep up with AI compute growth.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fi12xn3c2b7bjw9xa4y6w.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fi12xn3c2b7bjw9xa4y6w.png" alt=" " width="800" height="679"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SPAN, XFRA DATA METRIC FOR HOME POWER USAGE&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;How will it all work in practice? Here’s what SPAN has to say:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;XFRA converts available electrical headroom at the edge into high-demand compute&lt;br&gt;
by pairing cutting-edge GPU capacity with real-time energy visibility and control.&lt;br&gt;
Workloads are coordinated through the XFRA Secure Orchestration Layer (XSOL), which securely connects compute offtake customers to the fleet and makes many&lt;br&gt;
independent Nodes behave like a coherent cloud.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbjnodgxswmvffb3qn5ab.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fbjnodgxswmvffb3qn5ab.png" alt=" " width="800" height="553"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SPAN, XFRA ARCHITECTURE&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Here’s their breakdown for the individual nodes.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;An XFRA Node is built as a repeatable deployment unit, composed of one or more&lt;br&gt;
XFRA GPU Compute Modules, a local management gateway and thermal&lt;br&gt;
management designed for reliable, homeowner-friendly operation. The Compute&lt;br&gt;
Module is purpose-built and equipped with 8 cutting-edge, enterprise-grade GPUs,&lt;br&gt;
and ample CPU, memory, high-speed storage and networking bandwidth for optimized operation for the target workloads. The Compute Modules are liquid-cooled for quiet residential operation and to increase hardware and system&lt;br&gt;
reliability. Nodes are installed alongside a SPAN smart panel and a whole-home&lt;br&gt;
battery Energy Storage System (ESS) and can integrate rooftop solar where&lt;br&gt;
advantageous (and homeowner-approved).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This configuration is designed to support always-on compute within verified&lt;br&gt;
residential capacity while providing resilience during outages and short-duration&lt;br&gt;
disturbances. The ESS provides local buffering and backup power, improving&lt;br&gt;
continuity for both the home and the Node during power events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fnscimphe4wrg7htoorrr.png" class="article-body-image-wrapper"&gt;&lt;img src="https://media2.dev.to/dynamic/image/width=800%2Cheight=%2Cfit=scale-down%2Cgravity=auto%2Cformat=auto/https%3A%2F%2Fdev-to-uploads.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fuploads%2Farticles%2Fnscimphe4wrg7htoorrr.png" alt=" " width="799" height="337"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;SPAN, XFRA NODE ARCHITECTURE&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;While the XFRA project is not a direct replacement for data centers and the intentions behind this project are not yet clear what can be said is that they have been innovating in the field for a long time. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;


Why Does it Matter?
&lt;/h3&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Why did I choose to highlight companies such as Nous Research and SPAN? Our world is being shaped as we speak and now more than ever it is important to research the alternative ways to develop and train AI. From Open Source projects to brand new ideas creating a competitive culture with open flow of information, encouraging innovation is how tech has made it this far. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Transparency is often the difference between a dystopian future and one that encourages innovation and policies that support our communities not just take advantage of them. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So, no matter what you decide to do after reading this article I encourage you to build, innovate, and collaborate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;


Closing Remarks
&lt;/h2&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Thank you for your time and patience making it this far. I started writing this article after a conversation with a friend and poured the next three days into researching and applying personal experience to creating a comprehensive introduction on utilizing AI. This document can be shared with family and friends of all professional backgrounds in order to stop using AI and start utilizing it. &lt;/p&gt;

